// The reference checks AT THE DECLARATION that every field of a `@debug` struct
// is itself printable. The port had no such check at all - the message does not
// occur in its source once - so the program compiled and emitted a call to a
// printer that was never synthesised. The reader's build failed at the linker on
// a symbol they never wrote.
struct Plain { v: int }
@debug struct O { i: Plain }
fn main() { let o: O = O { i: Plain { v: 1 } }; println(o); }
